# Claude Code OAuth token — get one by running `claude setup-token` on your host.
# Lets the agent use your Claude subscription instead of an API key.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key instead — uncomment and fill in:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# Every key in this file is passed into the sandbox. Don't add a GitHub token:
# agents never reach GitHub, and the host refuses to start while GH_TOKEN or
# GITHUB_TOKEN is set here. The host uses its own `gh` login instead.
#
# A local run needs a queue scope, set on the command line rather than here
# (this file reaches the sandbox, and the host would refuse a push whose diff
# mentions a value from it):
# SANDCASTLE_ISSUE=<n> pnpm run sandcastle         builds only issue #n and its PR
# SANDCASTLE_LABEL=<label> pnpm run sandcastle     works the issues labelled <label>, e.g. Sandcastle:dev
# In GitHub Actions the queue is always the Sandcastle label, and setting
# either variable there stops the run.
#
# The run's time budget in minutes, also set on the command line or in the
# workflow's env rather than here (the host reads it from its own environment).
# No new round or role run starts once it has passed since the run started:
# SANDCASTLE_BUDGET_MINUTES=240 pnpm run sandcastle   (the default is 240)
